  "recovery": "Initial focused checks found an inaccessible Time means label because the label wrapped select option text. The corrected label and numbered event descriptions addressed that failure and duplicate-title ambiguity. A fixed-clock browser test then stalled renderer initialization on both projects; the identical product passed after removing the clock mock while retaining deterministic schedule dates and device-local today assertions. The exact internal clock interaction was not isolated. That successful run exposed a mobile heading clipped by upstream vertical centering. Top-aligning mobile slides restored heading access, with stronger full-bounds checks for heading, date and scrolled provenance. A final compact scheduled footer made the numbered legend and all three event controls fit in the phone viewport. Earlier failed and successful superseded runs remain fingerprinted and excluded from final counts. An initial read-only production schema export returned authentication error10000; account identity was confirmed and the unchanged read-only retry succeeded, without credential rotation or production mutation.\n\nPreserved successful superseded runs: schedule-focus3 at 829a07ec4a34760a6311e9fcce67a1a45ad8b45b, schedule-focus4 at ae712f110d35713edc1fcc90c2e38ee5a72cced8. Their receipt and log fingerprints are retained in the JSON record; none contributes to accepted-source validation counts. Passing test results alone did not establish release acceptance.",
